lty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14003808/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "fe7df6c88a014d695080775b76173688c0480606ebaf0a16084be0040ca46071"} {"question" "q-84947" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14003808/state.json" "file_sha256" "88415b4158500e5ce1577f1e58c689d1c240d8fa736de2af5777198a7f4305ad"} {"question" "q-84947" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "(-3,0)"] ["math" "(0,-3)"] ["math" "(0,0)"] ["math" "(0,3)"] ["math" "(3,0)"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14003808/state.json" "file_sha256" "88415b4158500e5ce1577f1e58c689d1c240d8fa736de2af5777198a7f4305ad"} {"question" "q-84947" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "(3,0)"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14003808/state.json" "file_sha256" "88415b4158500e5ce1577f1e58c689d1c240d8fa736de2af5777198a7f4305ad"} {"question" "q-84966" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "What are the coordinates of the vertex of the parabola ${x}^{2}=-\\frac{3}{2}(y-1)?$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14003808/state.json" "file_sha256" "88415b4158500e5ce1577f1e58c689d1c240d8fa736de2af5777198a7f4305ad"} {"question" "q-84966" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "The standard equation of an upward- or downward-opening parabola that has its vertex at $(h,k)$ is\n\n$$\n(x-h)^{2}=4p(y-k),\n$$\n\nwhere $p$ is constant.\n\nWe can rewrite the given equation as\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(x-0)^{2} & =4(-\\frac{3}{8})(y-1).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIt is now clear that our equation is of the standard type with $p=-\\frac{3}{8}.$\n\nComparing our equation with the standard equation, we can see that we have $h=0$ and $k=1.$ Therefore, the coordinates of the vertex of the parabola are $(0,1).$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14003808/state.json" "file_sha256" "88415b4158500e5ce1577f1e58c689d1c240d8fa736de2af5777198a7f4305ad"} {"question" "q-84966" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14003808/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "fe7df6c88a014d695080775b76173688c0480606ebaf0a16084be0040ca46071"} {"question" "q-84966" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14003808/state.json" "file_sha256" "88415b4158500e5ce1577f1e58c689d1c240d8fa736de2af5777198a7f4305ad"} {"question" "q-84966" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "(-2,3)"] ["math" "(-3,2)"] ["math" "(0,-1)"] ["math" "(0,1)"] ["math" "(1,0)"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14003808/state.json" "file_sha256" "88415b4158500e5ce1577f1e58c689d1c240d8fa736de2af5777198a7f4305ad"} {"question" "q-84966" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "(0,1)"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14003808/state.json" "file_sha256" "88415b4158500e5ce1577f1e58c689d1c240d8fa736de2af5777198a7f4305ad"} {"question" "q-115908" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "What are the coordinates of the vertex of the parabola ${y}^{2}=-32x?$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14003808/state.json" "file_sha256" "88415b4158500e5ce1577f1e58c689d1c240d8fa736de2af5777198a7f4305ad"} {"question" "q-115908" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "The standard equation of a left- or right-opening parabola that has its vertex at the origin is\n\n$$\n{y}^{2}=4px,\n$$\n\nwhere $p$ is a constant.\n\nWe can rewrite the given equation as \n\n$$\n{y}^{2}=4(-8)x.\n$$\n\nIt is now clear that our equation is of the standard type with $p=-8.$ Therefore, our parabola has its vertex at $(0,0).$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14003808/state.json" "file_sha256" "88415b4158500e5ce1577f1e58c689d1c240d8fa736de2af5777198a7f4305ad"} {"question" "q-115908" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14003808/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "fe7df6c88a014d695080775b76173688c0480606ebaf0a16084be0040ca46071"} {"question" "q-115908" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14003808/state.json" "file_sha256" "88415b4158500e5ce1577f1e58c689d1c240d8fa736de2af5777198a7f4305ad"} {"question" "q-115908" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "(-32,0)"] ["math" "(0,-8)"] ["math" "(0,0)"] ["math" "(0,32)"] ["math" "(8,0)"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14003808/state.json" "file_sha256" "88415b4158500e5ce1577f1e58c689d1c240d8fa736de2af5777198a7f4305ad"} {"question" "q-115908" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "(0,0)"